{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-163053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=15{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}$ is enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{2}$ and the line $y=1$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/28a3f0e1eda23169a649276a9cde34d3d96cdd75d5b2bc71c3535604612526e5.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=15{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 15{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}15{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{2}{5}{y}^{5/2}]}_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}(1-|x{|}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}-6{x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{8}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(2-\\frac{3}{4})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{y}$ is enclosed between the curve $y=2-{x}^{2}$ and  the line $y=1$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/2d08bcbbcd7ec4d8c388d24728c3f3afdc7c954497f342e9ac2b459fad24e5d2.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{3}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{x}^{2}}3\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3[y]_{y=1}^{y=2-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3[2-{x}^{2}-1]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[3x-{x}^{3}]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(3-1)-(-3+1) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-162984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}-15{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[5{x}^{3}-3{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-162974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le x,\\,0\\le x\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=3xy.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=3xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 3xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot {[{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-162919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,1\\le x\\le {e}^{y}}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{y}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{x=1}^{x={e}^{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-162977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-162977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163154" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x$ is enclosed between the line $y=4x$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163154" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/07701125c6acc36d127556bf95940bf0f74ba9ef3072f3af22dac26edc053a74.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4x}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{y=0}^{y=4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163154" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163154" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163154" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163154" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=5xy.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=5xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 5xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3y}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y{\\int }_{0}^{3y}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=3y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y(9{y}^{3}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}45{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[9{y}^{5}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163066" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163066" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163066" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2y$ is enclosed between the line $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/ddc11fc93f034c3d650854e21f178716c941c18f12eb94123e1af2c835c47981.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=2y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163155" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163155" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163155" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 0}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2{e}^{y}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=2{e}^{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{0}2x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{0}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{y=0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x-2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=1/2}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{2}{3})-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163062" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163062" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163062" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163152" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163152" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[x]_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}1-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1/2}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{1}{3})-(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{24}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163152" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163152" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163152" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163152" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{24}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ and is enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{3}$ and the $x$-axis for $1\\le x\\le 2.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $2$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/b6e8af58b8e7ba5f909d226b895bb39b3fc94e53686e4718eb32c9bb4ee61c08.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.$ \n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot [y]_{y=0}^{y={x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y$ and is enclosed between the curve $x=2y$ and the $y$-axis for $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{4}{3}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/3097e540292efd601743ba8de24acffc3b51469e77561b2bccbd799d1125e1ed.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y.$ \n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot (x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}+xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{x}^{2}+xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14{y}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7{y}^{4}}{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{7}{6})}{(\\frac{4}{3})}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=4xy.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $21$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 4xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}4x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4x{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4x{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{8}}{6}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{256}{6}-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{85}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{85}{2})}{21}=\\frac{85}{42}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-39020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{155}{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{44}{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{75}{42}"] ["math" "\\frac{85}{42}"] ["math" "\\frac{91}{42}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{85}{42}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{e}^{-y}\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $2$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{{e}^{-y}}^{1}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{x={e}^{-y}}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}0-(-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)={y}^{2}$ and is enclosed between the curve $x=1-{y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{4}{15}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/78f9da3d48727d2cb3c447be0f4050a044c4aabe29179fd31f04cd7b6c66eabd.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1-{y}^{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)={y}^{2}.$ \n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot (1-2{y}^{2}+{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{2}-2{y}^{4}+{y}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}-2{y}^{4}+{y}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{2}{5}{y}^{5}+\\frac{1}{7}{y}^{7}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{105}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{8}{105})}{(\\frac{4}{15})}=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-39547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{11}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{13}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis for $-2\\le y\\le 0.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\pi ,$ find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/14c292e8a224b59c143d0e8a57d43b554ce298cd4f44fc2169f516d683e8c35a.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}},\\,-2\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{4-{y}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}4-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{[4y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }[0-(-8+\\frac{8}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{4}{\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{8\\pi }{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-x\\le y\\le x}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $4$ square units, find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x{\\int }_{-x}^{x}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x[y]_{y=-x}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-39540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-39540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0\\le y\\le 4}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $\\frac{16}{3}$ square units, find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163289" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163289" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163289" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $\\pi $ square units, find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{[4x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }(8-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x={y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-2\\le y\\le 0.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{8}{3},$ find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/a8c57b12334a23542bae73ba1ac6848e69830b9663a1f83b6340f6812974f416.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-2\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}y\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y[x]_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y({y}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot (0-4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57c058db200f202cc38ca3fd9da42d887b8f8f08b619a25872495eb98ccf9724"} {"question" "q-163504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{6}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{8}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "q-163504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a14141923fef97da016288dafc9ceadc9e87d29a0c68af49789dd74371a125a"} {"question" "e-12470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin plate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/3cfabe3c702883ca24c3188908c4cefeee43adb30797308828edd98374b5b44f.png) with the mass density function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/ac38ea36432f3e278a4c2deb9203fbd5e486e348976e79157a5c6885a576f656.png) is enclosed between the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/65b9fa371f35bfa31a21b50bc02f64561e4c838d71ebd99bf2d2d1c1be196dff.png) and the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/1fd42a46221d9624ec3d81db0f5c73cd8428ee2f8d80b5d7e4ff67e7018fb194.png)-axis  for ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/11d74a99b97245c1998471b33f9b9d0974e251345f825c475db4079c02fa273a.png) Find the moment of the plate about the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/b63bded3ee2ad150f576fd05c209caf32bd34853f4a7132fe4ee85b59b06f61a.png)-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/example-12470.json" "file_sha256" "12eb14721abbd32bd738c06ba53a5c748f043ee64feecdd8edcefd25c877e933"} {"question" "e-12470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/05ff793b0aee1f05a79216f9e7f119afa544749c81077937f8f06a353f6ef4eb.png) with the mass density function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/bb3bf01e45585dbd5fe7732a1befa050d734bc46a466fea7f61f42851cfd3af8.png) about the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/d7d15efdd7573bd5b95e49ef05727ed1b8163a06781c393c1d3f27109fdc4eda.png)-axis is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/73a6e88adb05252ff114153227c13ae4f4adad9b676524179a20d9ae3d045d43.png)\n\nIn our case, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/33d4430552670d83a2c303e8ab286d3391f5611450f4e4f0b6ad6ccb58049b0e.png) is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/067543543031a1d8cb4ceb9a7901ad7db77629243adc6658d4a9eab3e98fe09f.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/03ccfab8b682725e94126f9fe59597d6e2886d3aeff64746681d0bbbed072520.png)\n\nand ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/17c342255c9bffbade441c02123bab3f7154e97b1a6a69a2874935f2dd684806.png) \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/ca38251cdd0a97967e8e6f4200e94b00571c5cfe2b84fef1991022e4fb976e62.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/example-12470.json" "file_sha256" "12eb14721abbd32bd738c06ba53a5c748f043ee64feecdd8edcefd25c877e933"} {"question" "e-12466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The lamina $D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\le x \\le y  ,\\, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/example-12466.json" "file_sha256" "379fc654dd6256fe4d82b2ce52dd23ce8c1619895edb1e492966478bcaa8fac5"} {"question" "e-12466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nM_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y .$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot {x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{0}^{y}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{y}^{5}}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{6}}{24}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/example-12466.json" "file_sha256" "379fc654dd6256fe4d82b2ce52dd23ce8c1619895edb1e492966478bcaa8fac5"} {"question" "e-8182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y) = x+y$ and is enclosed between the curve $y=x$ and the $x$-axis for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ units and its center of mass is located at $( \\overline{x}, \\overline{y} ),$ what is the value of $\\overline{y}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/example-8182.json" "file_sha256" "3946714450e53167bfe152069dcc5eeda4dfa9af03cda966eca766ffef6e47ac"} {"question" "e-8182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left( \\dfrac{M_y}{m}, \\dfrac{M_x}{m} \\right),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\iint \\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/b872242423692a20a9d50658c99d9e8cee7c9b2737fb96592bc2bc35b4f72c32.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:0 \\le x \\le 1, \\: 0 \\le y \\le x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda(x,y) = x+y.$ \n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot (x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}xy+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}xy+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)} = \\dfrac{5}{12}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/example-8182.json" "file_sha256" "3946714450e53167bfe152069dcc5eeda4dfa9af03cda966eca766ffef6e47ac"} {"question" "e-8183" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-y^2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/example-8183.json" "file_sha256" "6330c57ba905ae85d9c7fdac6d39ad1efd60bc6044b14fbfdf070379bea0bf76"} {"question" "e-8183" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area $A_D$ is given by $(x_c, y_c),$ where\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle x_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A, \\qquad \n\\displaystyle y_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/a7992c54f85f85cab3d9f923b8daca62c410393b364d30bcfbf5cff5efc93bbd.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{1-y^2}, \\: -1 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nA_D = \\dfrac12 \\cdot \\pi\\cdot 1^2 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(1-\\frac{1}{3})-(-1+\\frac{1}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/example-8183.json" "file_sha256" "6330c57ba905ae85d9c7fdac6d39ad1efd60bc6044b14fbfdf070379bea0bf76"}] "usage" {"q-39547" [] "e-8182" [] "q-39020" [] "e-8183" [] "e-12470" [] "q-39540" [] "q-162919" [] "e-12466" []} "basis" 2402 "retractions" [[17592186198556 :question/problem "The lamina $D = {(x, y): 0 \\le y \\le x, 0 \\le x \\le 1}$ has the mass density function $λ(x, y) = 3xy$. Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis."] [17592186198889 :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D = {(x, y): 1 \\le x \\le 2, 0 \\le y \\le x^{2}}$ and has the mass density function $λ(x, y) = 4xy$. Given that the mass of the lamina is $21$ units and its center of mass is located at $(x^(―), y^(―))$, what is the value of $y^(―)$?"] [17592186198902 :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $λ(x, y) = y^{2}$ and is enclosed between the curve $x = 1 - y^{2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\le y \\le 1$. Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{4}{15}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(x^(―), y^(―))$, what is the value of $x^(―)$?"] [17592186198901 :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D = {(x, y): 0 \\le x \\le 2,-x \\le y \\le x}$. Given that the area of the lamina is $4$ square units, find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid."] [17592186197977 :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y) = 2x$ is enclosed between the curve $y=1-x^2$ and the $x$-axis for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1$. Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis."] [17592186197977 :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nM_x = \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4166/Source/Images/7d803c99f95d817b7da87f748075ad7f.png)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\le x \\le 1, \\: 0 \\le y \\le 1-x^2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = 2x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{x} &= ∬_(D)y \\cdot 2xdA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)2xydA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1 - x^{2}}2xydydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}2x[∫_{0}^{1 - x^{2}}ydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}2x \\cdot [\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = 1 - x^{2}}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}x(1 - x^{2})^{2}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}x - 2x^{3} + x^{5}dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{2}x^{2} - \\frac{1}{2}x^{4} + \\frac{1}{6}x^{6}]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{6} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186197976 :question/problem "The lamina $D = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\le x \\le y,\\, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y$. Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis."] [17592186197976 :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nM_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{y} &= ∬_(D)x \\cdot x^{2}ydA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)x^{3}ydA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{y}x^{3}ydxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}y[∫_{0}^{y}x^{3}dx]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}y \\cdot [\\frac{x^{4}}{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = y}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}y \\cdot \\frac{y^{4}}{4}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{y^{5}}{4}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{6}}{24}]_{y = 0}^{y = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{24}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186198165 :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y) = x+y$ and is enclosed between the curve $y=x$ and the $x$-axis for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1$. Given that the mass of the plate is $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})$, what is the value of $\\overline{y}$?"] [17592186198165 :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left(\\dfrac{M_y}{m}, \\dfrac{M_x}{m} \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\iint \\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4166/Source/Images/00dd64e1a9f10365c732090d6562d731.png)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\:0 \\le x \\le 1, \\: 0 \\le y \\le x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = x+y\n$$\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{x} &= ∬_(D)yλ(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)y \\cdot (x + y)dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)xy + y^{2}dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{x}xy + y^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[\\frac{xy^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{3}}{3}]_{y = 0}^{y = x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}(\\frac{x^{3}}{2} + \\frac{x^{3}}{3})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}∫_{0}^{1}x^{3}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}[\\frac{1}{4}x^{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}(\\frac{1}{4} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{24}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)} = \\dfrac{5}{12}\n$$"] [17592186198166 :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-y^2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1$. Find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid."] [17592186198166 :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area $A_D$ is given by $(x_c, y_c)$, where\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle x_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A, \\qquad \\displaystyle y_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4166/Source/Images/d671a38e2ba00f523dee97b36289fe6a.png)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{1-y^2}, \\: -1 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nA_D = \\dfrac12 \\cdot \\pi\\cdot 1^2 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{c} &= \\frac{1}{A_{D}}∬_(D)xdA \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}}xdxdy \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}∫_{-1}^{1}[\\frac{x^{2}}{2}]_{x = 0}^{x = \\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}}dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}∫_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1 - y^{2}}{2}dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{π}∫_{-1}^{1}1 - y^{2}dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{π}[y - \\frac{y^{3}}{3}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{π}[(1 - \\frac{1}{3}) - (-1 + \\frac{1}{3})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{π} \\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{3π}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186194238 17592186194239 17592186194240 17592186194241 17592186194242 17592186197570 17592186197571 17592186197572 17592186197573 17592186197574 17592186197642 17592186197643 17592186197644 17592186197645 17592186197646 17592186197648 17592186197649 17592186197650 17592186197651 17592186197652] "immutable_fields" [[17592186194237 :answer-field/correct] [17592186194237 :answer-field/id] [17592186194237 :answer-field/key] [17592186194237 :answer-field/type] [17592186197569 :answer-field/correct] [17592186197569 :answer-field/id] [17592186197569 :answer-field/key] [17592186197569 :answer-field/type] [17592186197641 :answer-field/correct] [17592186197641 :answer-field/id] [17592186197641 :answer-field/key] [17592186197641 :answer-field/type] [17592186197647 :answer-field/correct] [17592186197647 :answer-field/id] [1759